Grok eventually produced a verified hard answer, so `n=56` cannot ship. The harness will complete the third hard call, then make the one allowed escalation to `n=60`, where the compact route is exactly at the 300-operation limit. If that also solves, the correct outcome is `cap_bound`, not a rejection.
