The first `n=60` oracle solved, so the initial ladder hits the no-tool operation cap. I’m not stopping at that provisional `cap_bound`: the prompt explicitly requires trying fixed-answer-length axes first. After this harness run closes, I’ll harden the same 168-atom witness by increasing the hidden modulus/number height while keeping `n=56` and the compact route length fixed, then rerun from a shifted ladder.
