codex
Implemented and verified a Track B generator based on [Theorem 9 of the paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.10717).

Key results:

- All G1–G9 gates pass.
- Shipping preset: `hard`, 56 regions and 168 item paths.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000.
- Reference algorithm: \(O(m^2)\), 28,224 measured operations.
- Bare oracle pool: 0/3 solved at shipping.
- Structural hint: 0/3 solved.
- Placebo hint: 1/3 solved.
- Answer size: 675 characters, 168 atoms.
- Intended compact route: 280 exact operations.

Deliverables:

- [gen_2506_10717.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10717/gen_2506_10717.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10717/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10717/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10717/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10717/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10717/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The README documents the important limitation: this verifies the paper’s canonical Theorem-9 drawing template using a succinct graph specification, not arbitrary 1-planarity drawings.
